  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so there is zero evidence and maximum uncertainty across all design dimensions (modality, encoder, profile setting, aggregation, fusion). The best first experiment is the simplest possible baseline: RNA-only, single profile, PCA-2000 encoder (config_001). This establishes a clean reference accuracy for the RNA signal alone with a standard, well-understood encoder and no aggregation/fusion complexity. It isolates the contribution of the RNA modality without confounding from learned encoders, multiprofile aggregation, or image fusion. With 9 experiments remaining, this baseline lets me subsequently test (a) whether image-only or multimodal configurations beat RNA-only, (b) whether learned encoders (scvi, scgpt) improve over PCA, and (c) whether multiprofile aggregation adds value. Starting with the simplest configuration maximizes the information gained per experiment by anchoring all future comparisons to a well-defined reference point."
}

